From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Benjamin Favre <ben@webdesign29.net>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 17:15:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Build: include stringstream for numeric locale formatting

Why: float_to_string_decimal_point constructs std::stringstream on non-Windows platforms. Apple libc++ only provides its forward declaration through the existing includes, so a build without precompiled headers fails. Include the complete definition where it is used.

Files: src/libslic3r/LocalesUtils.cpp

Upstreamable: yes

Co-Authored-By: Codex <noreply@openai.com>
---
 src/libslic3r/LocalesUtils.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/libslic3r/LocalesUtils.cpp b/src/libslic3r/LocalesUtils.cpp
index 9124f6e..7db5ca4 100644
--- a/src/libslic3r/LocalesUtils.cpp
+++ b/src/libslic3r/LocalesUtils.cpp
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
     #include <charconv>
 #endif
 #include <stdexcept>
+#include <sstream>
 
 #include <fast_float/fast_float.h>
 
